// para.synced (p2p P2) — a local `.merge()` publishes the new state to the topic, and another
// replica picks it up on `.sync()`. `a` and `b` are empty grow-only sets on "room"; `a` adds "x"
// (a local converge that also broadcasts), then `b` syncs and sees it. A CRDT has no "set" — you
// merge a delta and converge.
// expect: stdout "before: b has x = false"
// expect: stdout "after: b has x = true"
// expect: exit 0
use para.{crdt}
use para.synced.{synced_signal}

a = synced_signal(crdt.gset(), "room")
b = synced_signal(crdt.gset(), "room")

before = b.get().contains("x")
echo "before: b has x = ${before}"

a.merge(crdt.gset().insert("x"))
b.sync()

after = b.get().contains("x")
echo "after: b has x = ${after}"
